            "reviewer_id": "User_9719457_1_11",
            "review_title": "Review at Kebab Sai Gon",
            "review_text": "david o\n18 contributions\n0\nA land mark for most expats\nMay 2016\nBeen living in Vietnam for 10 years now and if there's one consistent thing I can find among the fellow expatriate community is it their love of the chicken kebab served at 'Kebab Sai Gon'. Trust me, it doesn't matter if you're French, Australian, American or British, any one who has tried the kebabs here will always come back. It's been around for years and is happy to do a steady business as a small street stall. The staff are friendly and very efficient and the price cannot be argued with, 27,000 vnd for the classic kebab, 32,000 vnd if you want extra meat. They are cheap, they are friendly, their kebabs are of consistent quality and they keep churning them out. Many kebab stalls in HCMC have come and gone due to lowering of standards, poor hygiene, bad business management BUT Kebab Sai Gon just keep the kebabs coming.\n\nI would say order the 32,000vnd chicken kebab and have it with the classic garlic sauce. You won't regret it. Best kebab, wait BEST sandwich in HCMC hands down.\nRead more\nWritten May 5, 2016",
